---
/**
 * CountryRules — three short labelled boxes with country-specific lending rules,
 * so the general text on global calculators stays country-neutral.
 * Used by the debt-to-income, credit-card payoff, loan affordability and mortgage pages.
 */
interface Props {
  id?: string;
}
const { id = 'country-rules' } = Astro.props;
---

<section aria-labelledby={id} class="mb-6">
  <h2 id={id} class="text-xl font-bold text-text-primary mb-4">Country rules at a glance</h2>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
    <div class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-card p-4">
      <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-text-primary mb-2">India</h3>
      <ul class="text-xs text-text-muted space-y-1.5 list-disc pl-4 leading-relaxed">
        <li>Banks cap the <strong>FOIR</strong> (fixed obligations to income ratio) at about <strong>40–50%</strong> of net monthly income, depending on income level and lender.</li>
        <li>A <strong>CIBIL</strong> score of 750+ usually gets the best rates.</li>
        <li><strong>18% GST</strong> is charged on credit card interest and fees.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-card p-4">
      <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-text-primary mb-2">United States</h3>
      <ul class="text-xs text-text-muted space-y-1.5 list-disc pl-4 leading-relaxed">
        <li>The <strong>28/36 guideline</strong>: housing up to 28% and all debts up to 36% of gross income.</li>
        <li>There has been <strong>no fixed Qualified Mortgage DTI cap</strong> since 2022 (CFPB replaced the 43% limit with a price-based test); limits come from each loan program and lender.</li>
        <li>Card minimum payments are typically <strong>1% of the balance plus interest and fees</strong>, or a fixed floor (often $25–$40), whichever is higher.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-card p-4">
      <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-text-primary mb-2">United Kingdom</h3>
      <ul class="text-xs text-text-muted space-y-1.5 list-disc pl-4 leading-relaxed">
        <li>Lenders must run an <strong>FCA affordability assessment</strong> of income and committed spending before lending.</li>
        <li>Card minimum payments must cover at least <strong>interest, fees and 1% of the balance</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>No VAT</strong> is charged on credit interest.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
